2. GRANT OF COMMERCIAL LICENSE & USAGE TIERS
================================================================================
2.1 Commercial License Grant:
Subject to full payment of applicable commercial subscription fees and strict compliance with this Agreement, ScanDrix grants Licensee a limited, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable, non-transferable license during the active subscription term to:
  (a) Install and run the compiled binary executable instances of the Software solely on authorized servers, cloud infrastructure, or local workstations;
  (b) Connect designated developer seats, pull request automation webhooks, and repository workflows up to the maximum seat and repository limit authorized in Licensee’s commercial schedule.

2.2 Enterprise Seat & Allocation Controls:
Licensee shall not allow access to the Software by any individuals other than Authorized Users. Developer seats cannot be shared, multiplexed, or transferred between distinct individuals without explicit administrative reassignment.

2.3 Evaluation & Internal Proof-of-Concept:
If the Software is provided under an evaluation or proof-of-concept designation, Licensee may use the Software solely for internal evaluation purposes for a period not exceeding thirty (30) days. Any production use, revenue-generating deployment, or integration into production CI/CD pipelines during evaluation is strictly prohibited.

