3. STRICT LICENSE RESTRICTIONS
================================================================================
Except to the extent expressly permitted by applicable law that cannot be contractually waived, Licensee shall not, directly or indirectly:
  (a) Copy, duplicate, clone, replicate, or reproduce the Software, in whole or in part, except for one (1) single machine-readable copy created solely for disaster recovery backup;
  (b) Modify, translate, adapt, alter, enhance, or create derivative works based upon the Software or any component thereof;
  (c) Reverse engineer, decompile, decrypt, disassemble, extract, or otherwise attempt to derive or reconstruct the source code, underlying logic, data formats, or internal algorithms of the Software;
  (d) Sublicense, sell, resell, lease, rent, loan, distribute, publish, transfer, assign, host as an outsourced service, or operate a service bureau / commercial code review SaaS utilizing the Software for third-party benefit;
  (e) Circumvent, disable, bypass, tamper with, or defeat any license entitlement keys, cryptographic signature checks (including Ed25519 tokens), rate limiters, or security verification features embedded within the Software;
  (f) Remove, alter, cover, or obscure any copyright, trademark, logo, watermark, confidentiality notice, or proprietary legend contained in or displayed by the Software;
  (g) Use the Software, output, prompts, heuristics, or rule catalogs to train, fine-tune, benchmark, evaluate, or develop any competing artificial intelligence, machine learning model, code review engine, or static analysis tooling;
  (h) Publish or publicly disclose any competitive performance metrics, benchmark comparisons, vulnerability disclosures, or penetration testing results without prior written authorization from ScanDrix.

