"Confidential Information" means all non-public information disclosed by ScanDrix to Licensee, including but not limited to the Software source code, internal system prompts, heuristic rule taxonomies, AST structures, database schemas, cryptographic protocols, pricing schedules, roadmaps, and business strategies.

4.2 Duty of Care:
Licensee agrees to safeguard ScanDrix's Confidential Information with at least the same degree of care it uses for its own most sensitive trade secrets, and in no event less than a reasonable degree of care. Licensee shall restrict access to Confidential Information strictly to employees and contractors who have a legitimate need-to-know and who are bound by written confidentiality obligations at least as restrictive as this Agreement.

4.3 Remedies for Breach:
Licensee acknowledges that any unauthorized disclosure or use of ScanDrix Confidential Information or source code will cause immediate, irreparable harm to ScanDrix for which monetary damages alone would be inadequate. Accordingly, ScanDrix shall be entitled to seek immediate injunctive relief, specific performance, and any other equitable remedies in any court of competent jurisdiction without the necessity of posting a bond.

